    "body": "Relay BB run pushed an update.\n\nPull request: #312\n\nTokens: 0 · Cost: $0.0000\n\nPushed successfully to `bb/relay-226-module-contract-10-12-author-manifests-thr_g9rv3jpz2n`.\n\n## Summary\n\nAuthored `ModuleManifest`s for issue #226's four target modules — a pure retrofit, no behavior or data changes:\n\n- **`schemaCore`** (`backend/packages/data/src/chokePoint/schemaCoreModuleManifest.ts`) — the choke point and core system tables (`0001_core_schema.sql`). No databases, no agent tools.\n- **`views`** (`backend/packages/data/src/views/viewsModuleManifest.ts`) — `0002_views.sql` and the built-in view types (`table`, `board`, `calendar`, `list`).\n- **`docs`** (`backend/packages/data/src/docs/docsModuleManifest.ts`) — `0003_docs.sql`, the block-append mechanism. Deliberately doesn't redeclare `DOC_COMPACTION_SWEEP`/etc. since those remain core cron tasks.\n- **`systemDatabases`** (`backend/packages/data/src/seed/systemDatabasesModuleManifest.ts`) — the ten hardcoded databases from `seedTenDatabases.ts`, reusing their existing `owner_module_id` keys and names, plus Journal's `temporal-switcher` view type.\n\nEach manifest is re-exported from the `@semprec/data` package barrel. A new integration-tier test file, `backend/packages/data/src/__tests__/coreModuleManifests.test.ts`, verifies each manifest loads through `ModuleRegistry.loadModule()`, passes structural validation, and that all four load together into one registry with no id/name/key collisions.\n\nNote: this worktree's branch had been forked from a `develop` tip that predated the whole module-contract series (parts 01–09), so before authoring anything I fast-forward-merged `origin/develop` (currently at PR #311) into this branch to bring in `@semprec/module-registry` and the rest of the infrastructure these manifests depend on.\n\nVerified: full build (`pnpm -r run build`) and all three test tiers pass — unit (83/83), integration (369/369, including the 5 new load tests), and e2e (5/5).\n\nRelay-Step-Status: pass",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
